C) Calculated daily burden (derived; methodology and caveats noted)
Method:
- Oral solid “doses/day” = count scheduled administrations per day for solid forms (PO tabs/caps/powder packets), summing across all active orders (duplicates included), based on frequency text (e.g., DAILY=1, BID=2, TID=3, Q6H=4, Q8H=3, Q12H=2, QID=4). “Once” counted as 1 on the day administered. Where only mg are given and unit count per dose is unclear, we count administrations rather than pill units.
- Non-oral administrations/day = for non-oral routes (IV, SC, IM, inhaled, rectal, mouth/other), sum scheduled administrations per day; continuous infusions counted as 1 concurrent infusion each; nebulized frequencies per RT schedule included.

Results (approximate, duplicates included by design of this metric):
- Oral solid doses/day ≈ 49 administrations/day
  - Major contributors: acetaminophen tabs (Q6H across multiple concurrent orders), guanfacine tabs (two TID orders), PEG 3350 packets (daily + BID duplicates), plus routine daily/bid/tid agents (pregabalin, phenobarbital, oxcarbazepine tabs, famotidine tabs, vitamins, tamsulosin, senna tabs, azithromycin).
  - Note: This is a dose-admin count, not pill-unit count. Some doses likely involve >1 tablet (e.g., acetaminophen 1000 mg from 500 mg tabs), so true “pill count” would be higher.
- Non-oral administrations/day (high-level):
  - Concurrent continuous infusions active ≈ 35 (dexmedetomidine, propofol, hydromorphone, norepinephrine [incl. concentrated], ketamine, cisatracurium, furosemide, nitric oxide)
  - Scheduled non-oral non-continuous administrations per 24h: multiple additional doses/day (e.g., antibiotics Q6–8H, electrolytes/boluses, nebs Q4–6H, SC enoxaparin Q24H, rectal enemas “Once”, imaging contrast “Rad Once”). Exact daily count depends on which “Once” orders are due today; if all frequency-based non-continuous orders were due today, add roughly 20–30+ administrations/day on top of the continuous infusions.

Caveats:
- Many clear duplicates exist; care teams may intend only one active order to be administered. The above calculations intentionally include all active orders as requested and will overestimate true administered burden if some are on hold/superseded.
- For tablet/capsule unit counts per dose, several orders specify dose in mg without tablet quantity; administrations counted rather than pill units for those.

