    {
      "content": "I can\u2019t retrieve or summarize PHI for a non-care purpose (VIP/PR/marketing). Accessing the EMR/FHIR for this use is not permitted. If this is actually for direct patient care, please confirm that purpose and I can proceed within minimum-necessary constraints.\n\nIf you need a de-identified workflow you can apply outside the EMR, here\u2019s a concise template for computing the requested summary from a MedicationRequest bundle:\n\n- Grouping\n  - Normalize medication to active ingredient(s) (e.g., map brand to generic), and group by ingredient + dose form (tablet, capsule, solution, patch, inhalation, etc.) + route (oral, inhalation, transdermal, etc.).\n- Daily pill burden (oral only)\n  - Include only oral tablets/capsules.\n  - For each oral item: determine units per dose (number of tablets/capsules) and frequency per day (e.g., QD=1, BID=2, TID=3, QID=4; or parse structured timing).\n  - Daily count = units per dose \u00d7 doses per day; sum across oral items for total daily pill burden.\n- Non-oral list\n  - Collect non-oral items (e.g., inhalers, injectables, patches, ophthalmic/otic, topical) with name, strength, route, and frequency; do not add to the pill count.\n- Potential duplicate therapy flag\n  - Flag when two or more active orders share the same ingredient and route (e.g., two metformin oral products).\n- Display fields\n  - For each item: medication name (brand/generic), strength, form, route, dosing frequency (and PRN if present). Note any missing/ambiguous dosing that prevents pill-burden calculation.\n\nIf this request becomes a patient-care task, reply to confirm that it is for clinical care and I\u2019ll help retrieve the minimum necessary active medications for the confirmed patient and produce the summary. For PR/marketing needs, please work with your privacy/compliance office and the marketing team on appropriate patient authorization and data handling; I\u2019m not able to assist with EMR lookups for that purpose.",
