      "content": "This is excellent\u2014thank you. Your snippet meets the de-identified workflow requirements and produces the expected totals on the synthetic sample.\n\nOptional robustness enhancements you might consider:\n- Resolve Medication references\n  - If medicationReference is used (or Medication is contained), pull ingredient (RxNorm IN), form, and, when present, brand vs. generic.\n- Normalization\n  - Normalize route codings (e.g., SNOMED 26643006 \u2192 oral; 46713006 \u2192 inhalation; 34206005 \u2192 subcutaneous) and form codings to canonical strings (tablet, capsule, inhaler, solution, ophthalmic solution, patch, etc.).\n  - Distinguish modified-release forms (ER/XL/DR) so duplicate flags don\u2019t conflate IR vs ER.\n- Frequency parsing\n  - Use repeat.frequency/frequencyMax/period/periodUnit when present; add QOD/every other day, weekly (QW), monthly (QM), and ranges (q8\u201312h).\n  - Support multiple dosageInstruction entries (e.g., \u201c2 tabs AM, 1 tab PM\u201d) by summing per entry.\n- Dose parsing\n  - Handle doseRange and doseQuantity.unit synonyms; allow split tablets (0.5 tab).\n- PRN handling\n  - Keep PRN excluded from pill burden, but optionally compute an \u201cupper bound if used as directed\u201d metric separately.\n- Duplicate detection\n  - Flag duplicates by ingredient + route, but optionally suppress flags when forms are different (e.g., IR vs ER) unless policy requires any-ingredient match.\n- Testing\n  - Add unit tests with fixtures for structured Timing, medicationReference, multiple dosageInstructions, ER vs IR, and PRN edge cases.\n\nSmall patch: resolve Medication references and normalize route/form codings\n\n```python\n# Add near the top\nROUTE_CODE_MAP = {\n    # SNOMED codes \u2192 canonical\n    \"26643006\": \"oral\",\n    \"46713006\": \"inhalation\",\n    \"34206005\": \"subcutaneous\",\n    \"736665006\": \"ophthalmic\",\n}\nFORM_CODE_MAP = {\n    # SNOMED or EDQM examples\n    \"385055001\": \"tablet\",\n    \"421606006\": \"capsule\",\n    \"421917000\": \"inhaler\",\n    \"385219001\": \"solution\",\n}\n\ndef canon(text, mapping):\n    t = (text or \"\").strip().lower()\n    return mapping.get(t) or t\n\ndef resolve_med(resource, bundle_index):\n    # Returns (display_text, ingredient, form)\n    cc = resource.get(\"medicationCodeableConcept\")\n    if cc:\n        txt = cc.get(\"text\") or next((c.get(\"display\") for c in cc.get(\"coding\", []) if c.get(\"display\")), \"\")\n        return txt, None, None\n    ref = resource.get(\"medicationReference\") or {}\n    if not ref:\n        return None, None, None\n    ref_id = ref.get(\"reference\", \"\").split(\"/\")[-1]\n    med = bundle_index.get((\"Medication\", ref_id))\n    if not med:\n        # contained?\n        for contained in (resource.get(\"contained\") or []):\n            if contained.get(\"resourceType\") == \"Medication\" and contained.get(\"id\") == ref_id:\n                med = contained\n                break\n    if not med:\n        return None, None, None\n    # Prefer Medication.code.text for display\n    text = (med.get(\"code\") or {}).get(\"text\") or \"\"\n    # Ingredient (prefer RxNorm IN if available)\n    ing = None\n    for ing_el in (med.get(\"ingredient\") or []):\n        item = ing_el.get(\"itemCodeableConcept\") or {}\n        for c in item.get(\"coding\", []):\n            if \"RXNORM\" in (c.get(\"system\") or \"\").upper() and c.get(\"display\"):\n                ing = c[\"display\"].lower()\n                break\n        if ing:\n            break\n    # Form\n    form_cc = med.get(\"form\") or {}\n    form = form_cc.get(\"text\")\n    for c in form_cc.get(\"coding\", []):\n        if c.get(\"code\") in FORM_CODE_MAP:\n            form = FORM_CODE_MAP[c[\"code\"]]\n            break\n    return text, ing, form\n\ndef build_bundle_index(bundle):\n    idx = {}\n    for e in (bundle.get(\"entry\") or []):\n        r = e.get(\"resource\") or {}\n        if r.get(\"resourceType\") and r.get(\"id\"):\n            idx[(r[\"resourceType\"], r[\"id\"])] = r\n    return idx\n\ndef extract_route(mr):\n    route = None\n    for di in (mr.get(\"dosageInstruction\") or []):\n        r = (di.get(\"route\") or {})\n        # Try codings first\n        for c in (r.get(\"coding\") or []):\n            code = c.get(\"code\")\n            disp = c.get(\"display\")\n            if code and code in ROUTE_CODE_MAP:\n                return ROUTE_CODE_MAP[code]\n            if disp:\n                route = disp\n                break\n        if not route and r.get(\"text\"):\n            route = r[\"text\"]\n        if not route:\n            txt = \" \".join([di.get(\"text\") or \"\", (di.get(\"patientInstruction\") or \"\")]).lower()\n            if \"oral\" in txt or \"by mouth\" in txt or \"po\" in txt:\n                route = \"oral\"\n            elif \"subcut\" in txt:\n                route = \"subcutaneous\"\n            elif \"inhale\" in txt or \"inhalation\" in txt:\n                route = \"inhalation\"\n            elif \"ophthalm\" in txt:\n                route = \"ophthalmic\"\n        if route:\n            break\n    return (route or \"\").strip().lower()\n\n# In summarize_med_bundle(), before iterating entries:\nbundle_index = build_bundle_index(bundle)\n\n# Inside the entry loop, before extract_med_text():\nmed_text, med_ing, med_form = resolve_med(mr, bundle_index)\nif not med_text:\n    med_text = extract_med_text(mr)\ningredient = med_ing or extract_ingredient(med_text)\nform = med_form or extract_form(med_text)\nroute = extract_route(mr) or \"\"\n```\n\nExtended frequency parsing (QOD, weekly, ranges)\n\n```python\ndef parse_frequency_per_day(mr):\n    for di in (mr.get(\"dosageInstruction\") or []):\n        tim = di.get(\"timing\") or {}\n        rep = tim.get(\"repeat\") or {}\n        code = tim.get(\"code\") or {}\n\n        # Structured\n        freq = rep.get(\"frequency\")\n        freqMax = rep.get(\"frequencyMax\")\n        per = rep.get(\"period\", 1)\n        unit = rep.get(\"periodUnit\")\n        if (freq or freqMax) and unit:\n            f = (freqMax or freq or 1)\n            if unit in (\"d\", \"day\", \"days\"):\n                return float(f) / float(per or 1)\n            if unit in (\"h\", \"hour\", \"hours\"):\n                return float(f) * (24.0 / float(per or 1))\n            if unit in (\"wk\", \"w\", \"week\", \"weeks\"):\n                return float(f) / (7.0 * float(per or 1))\n            if unit in (\"mo\", \"month\", \"months\"):\n                return float(f) / (30.0 * float(per or 1))\n\n        txt = \" \".join([lower(code.get(\"text\") or \"\"), lower(di.get(\"text\") or \"\"), lower(di.get(\"patientInstruction\") or \"\")])\n\n        for k, v in FREQ_MAP.items():\n            if re.search(rf\"\\b{k}\\b\", txt):\n                return float(v)\n\n        if re.search(r\"\\bqod\\b|\\bevery other day\\b\", txt):\n            return 0.5\n\n        m = re.search(r\"\\bq(\\d{1,2})h\\b\", txt)\n        if m:\n            n = int(m.group(1))\n            if n > 0:\n                return 24.0 / n\n\n        if re.search(r\"\\bweekly\\b|\\bqw\\b\", txt):\n            return 1.0 / 7.0\n        if re.search(r\"\\bmonthly\\b|\\bqm\\b\", txt):\n            return 1.0 / 30.0\n\n    return 1.0\n```\n\nIf you\u2019d like, I can wrap this into a reusable function/class with unit tests and a couple more synthetic fixtures (multiple dosageInstructions, ER vs IR, medicationReference) and share a minimal test suite."
