      "content": "Got it. I\u2019ll stay within the non-PHI, de-identified/export support scope.\n\nHere\u2019s what I can provide now:\n- Runtime-tailorable mappings: ready (route/form/freq/ingredient JSONs from prior message).\n- Duplicate policy: default = suppress IR vs ER; toggle via flag.\n- Packaging: minimal Dockerfile + Makefile.\n- Scale: optional ijson-based streaming mode so your team can summarize large, authorized exports via stdin with low memory.\n\nBelow are safe, drop-in patches you can apply to your existing summarizer/CLI. They don\u2019t access any EMR; they only operate on an authorized Bundle export you provide.\n\n1) Summarizer: add a streaming-capable entry point\n- Adds summarize_resources(resources_iter, med_index=None) so the CLI can feed resources as they stream in.\n- Keeps your current logic and duplicate policy.\n\nPatch (add to medsummarizer.py)\n- Add a helper to process a single MedicationRequest (re-uses your current logic).\n\ndef summarize_medrequest(self, mr, med_index=None):\n    # med_index: optional {(resourceType, id): resource} for Medication refs\n    if not mr or mr.get(\"resourceType\") != \"MedicationRequest\":\n        return None\n    status = (mr.get(\"status\") or \"\").strip().lower()\n    if status != \"active\":\n        return None\n\n    # Build a minimal index if provided\n    idx = med_index or {}\n    med_text, med_ings, med_form = resolve_medication(mr, idx)\n    if not med_text:\n        med_text = extract_med_text(mr)\n    route = extract_route(mr)\n    form = med_form or extract_form_from_text(med_text)\n    strength = extract_strength(med_text) or \"\"\n\n    per_di_freq_labels = []\n    daily_pills = 0.0\n    prn_upper_oral = 0.0\n    any_prn = False\n    for di in (mr.get(\"dosageInstruction\") or []):\n        di_prn = is_prn_di(di)\n        any_prn = any_prn or di_prn\n        units = parse_units_per_dose(di)\n        freq = parse_freq_per_day(di)\n        per_di_freq_labels.append(freq_label_from_