            "effectiveDateTime": "2023-11-13T07:00:00Z",
            "issued": "2023-11-13T07:00:00Z",
            "valueQuantity": null,
            "interpretation": [
              {
                "coding": null,
                "text": "Medication reconciliation performed prior to morning rounds at 07:00 on 2023-11-13."
              }
            ],
            "valueString": "Computed medication reconciliation summary (from active MedicationRequests)\n- Scope: GET /MedicationRequest?patient=S1733937&status=active returned 70+ active orders. Below I:\n  - grouped by ingredient/form/route,\n  - calculated daily tablet/capsule burden (see method notes),\n  - and flagged potential ingredient-duplicates.\n\nMethod notes for pill burden\n- Count only oral tablets/capsules.\n- Frequencies used: DAILY/QAM/QHS/nightly = 1/day; BID = 2/day; TID = 3/day; weekly = 1/7\u22480.143/day; 2x/week = 2/7\u22480.286/day; TU/TH/SU or TU/TH/SA = 3/7\u22480.429/day; M/W/F = 3/7\u22480.429/day.\n- If the order explicitly states tablet count (unit \u201cTablet\u201d), I used that (e.g., Bactrim \u201c2 Tablet\u201d). If dose is in mg and tablet strength isn\u2019t explicit or conflicts, I count 1 tablet per administration and flag the inconsistency.\n\nGrouped list (ingredient \u2013 form \u2013 route \u2013 active orders snapshot)\n- Prednisone \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 5 mg daily (multiple active); 10 mg daily; 20 mg daily. Potential duplicates/taper overlap.\n- Tacrolimus \u2013 capsule \u2013 oral: 0.5 mg TU/TH/SU (duplicates present); 0.5 mg 2\u00d7/week. Potential duplicate schedules.\n- Sirolimus \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 0.5 mg Q7 days; 0.5 mg TU/TH/SA. Potential duplicate schedules.\n- Amlodipine \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 5 mg daily.\n- Empagliflozin \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 10 mg daily; 25 mg daily. Potential duplicate strengths.\n- Escitalopram \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 5 mg daily (duplicates present); 10 mg tablet order with a recorded 5 mg dose (inconsistency).\n- Rosuvastatin \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 5 mg nightly (duplicates present; one entry shows 2.5 mg dose with 5 mg tab). Potential duplicate/possible tablet-splitting.\n- Ferrous sulfate \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 325 mg daily (duplicates present).\n- Folic acid \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 1 mg daily (duplicates present).\n- Diltiazem \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 30 mg TID.\n- Pantoprazole \u2013 enteric-coated tablet \u2013 oral: 40 mg BID AC; 40 mg QAM AC. Potential duplicate regimens.\n- Valganciclovir \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 450 mg QAM (duplicates present).\n- Azathioprine \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 50 mg daily (duplicates present).\n- Sulfamethoxazole\u2013trimethoprim \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 800-160 mg M/W/F: 2 tablets (newer); also 1 tablet (older). Potential duplicate/conflicting dose.\n- Azithromycin \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 250 mg M/W/F (duplicates present).\n- Posaconazole DR \u2013 enteric-coated tablet \u2013 oral: 100 mg tablets to total 300 mg QAM (duplicates present).\n- Calcium carbonate\u2013vitamin D3 \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 500 mg\u20135 mcg BID (duplicates present).\n- Levetiracetam \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 500 mg BID (duplicates present; dose field shows 1000 mg\u2014see inconsistency).\n- Sitagliptin \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 100 mg daily.\n- Pravastatin \u2013 tablet \u2013 oral: 40 mg daily.\n\nNon-oral or non-tablet/capsule actives (not counted in pill burden; still present/duplicated)\n- Remdesivir IVPB (200 mg once + 100 mg Q24H, multiple entries).\n- Enoxaparin SC Q24H (duplicates).\n- Insulin lispro SC (meal scale TID, bedtime QHS, NPO Q6H) \u2013 multiple insulin orders by context.\n- Inhaled therapies: fluticasone furoate\u2013vilanterol DSDV (duplicates), ipratropium\u2013albuterol, albuterol nebs.\n- Patch: lidocaine 5% TD Q24H.\n- Various one-time IVs (e.g., cefepime, piperacillin\u2013tazobactam), dextrose IV, NS bolus.\n- Apheresis-related heparin solutions and alteplase (multiple dates).\n- Methoxsalen injection (multiple dates).\n- Administrative/template entry: \u201cZZZ IMS TEMPLATE\u201d (appears non-clinical; excluding from burden).\n\nPill burden (tablets/capsules per day)\n- Deduplicated by ingredient (keeping the most current regimen per ingredient):\n  - Prednisone 1/day\n  - Tacrolimus ~0.429/day (TU/TH/SU)\n  - Sirolimus ~0.143/day (weekly)\n  - Amlodipine 1/day\n  - Empagliflozin 1/day\n  - Escitalopram 1/day\n  - Rosuvastatin 1/day\n  - Ferrous sulfate 1/day\n  - Folic acid 1/day\n  - Diltiazem 3/day\n  - Pantoprazole 2/day\n  - Valganciclovir 1/day\n  - Azathioprine 1/day\n  - Sulfamethoxazole\u2013trimethoprim ~0.857/day (2 tablets M/W/F)\n  - Azithromycin ~0.429/day (M/W/F)\n  - Posaconazole DR 3/day (3 \u00d7 100 mg)\n  - Calcium/Vitamin D 2/day\n  - Levetiracetam 2/day (assumed 1 tab BID)\n  - Sitagliptin 1/day\n  - Pravastatin 1/day\n- Total average daily tablets/capsules (deduplicated): \u224823.9/day.\n  - Baseline on non-M/W/F days (excluding intermittent contributions): \u224823/day.\n  - On M/W/F: baseline + (Bactrim 2 + Azithro 1) \u2248 26/day.\n  - Tacrolimus days add +1; weekly sirolimus day adds +1 (ranges 23\u201327/day depending on day-of-week).\n- If counting every active order including obvious duplicates, the theoretical total is much higher (inflated by duplicate entries).\n\nPotential ingredient-duplicate flags (examples)\n- Prednisone; Tacrolimus; Sirolimus\n- Posaconazole DR; Pantoprazole\n- Escitalopram; Rosuvastatin\n- Ferrous sulfate; Folic acid; Valganciclovir; Azathioprine\n- Levetiracetam; Sulfamethoxazole\u2013trimethoprim; Azithromycin\n- Calcium carbonate\u2013vitamin D3\n- Remdesivir IV (loading + maintenance both active)\n- Insulin lispro (meal/bedtime/NPO scales all active)\n- Fluticasone furoate\u2013vilanterol inhaler\n- Enoxaparin\n\nData quality/inconsistencies to review\n- Escitalopram 10 mg PO tabs recorded with dose 5 mg.\n- Rosuvastatin 5 mg PO tabs recorded with dose 2.5 mg (possible half-tablet).\n- Levetiracetam 500 mg PO tabs BID recorded with a 1000 mg dose value (may reflect total daily vs per-dose).\n- Multiple overlapping prednisone strengths suggest taper remnants.\n- \u201cZZZ IMS TEMPLATE\u201d appears non-medication."
