g., cefepime, piperacillin\u2013tazobactam), dextrose IV, NS bolus.\n- Apheresis-related heparin solutions and alteplase (multiple dates).\n- Methoxsalen injection (multiple dates).\n- Administrative/template entry: \u201cZZZ IMS TEMPLATE\u201d (appears non-clinical; excluding from burden).\n\nPill burden (tablets/capsules per day)\n- Deduplicated by ingredient (keeping the most current regimen per ingredient):\n  - Prednisone 1/day\n  - Tacrolimus ~0.429/day (TU/TH/SU)\n  - Sirolimus ~0.143/day (weekly)\n  - Amlodipine 1/day\n  - Empagliflozin 1/day\n  - Escitalopram 1/day\n  - Rosuvastatin 1/day\n  - Ferrous sulfate 1/day\n  - Folic acid 1/day\n  - Diltiazem 3/day\n  - Pantoprazole 2/day\n  - Valganciclovir 1/day\n  - Azathioprine 1/day\n  - Sulfamethoxazole\u2013trimethoprim ~0.857/day (2 tablets M/W/F)\n  - Azithromycin ~0.429/day (M/W/F)\n  - Posaconazole DR 3/day (3 \u00d7 100 mg)\n  - Calcium/Vitamin D 2/day\n  - Levetiracetam 2/day (assumed 1 tab BID)\n  - Sitagliptin 1/day\n  - Pravastatin 1/day\n- Total average daily tablets/capsules (deduplicated): \u224823.9/day.\n  - Baseline on non-M/W/F days (excluding intermittent contributions): \u224823/day.\n  - On M/W/F: baseline + (Bactrim 2 + Azithro 1) \u2248 26/day.\n  - Tacrolimus days add +1; weekly sirolimus day adds +1 (ranges 23\u201327/day depending on day-of-week).\n- If counting every active order including obvious duplicates, the theoretical total is much higher (inflated by duplicate entries).\n\nPotential ingredient-duplicate flags (examples)\n- Prednisone; Tacrolimus; Sirolimus\n- Posaconazole DR; Pantoprazole\n- Escitalopram; Rosuvastatin\n- Ferrous sulfate; Folic acid; Valganciclovir; Azathioprine\n- Levetiracetam; Sulfamethoxazole\u2013trimethoprim; Azithromycin\n- Calcium carbonate\u2013vitamin D3\n- Remdesivir IV (loading + maintenance both active)\n- Insulin lispro (meal/bedtime/NPO scales all active)\n- Fluticasone furoate\u2013vilanterol inhaler\n- Enoxaparin\n\nData quality/inconsistencies to review\n- Escitalopram 10 mg PO tabs recorded with dose 5 mg.\n- Rosuvastatin 5 mg PO tabs recorded with dose 2.5 mg (possible half-tablet).\n- Levetiracetam 500 mg PO tabs BID recorded with a 1000 mg dose value (may reflect total daily vs per-dose).\n- Multiple overlapping prednisone strengths suggest taper remnants.\n- \u201cZZZ IMS TEMPLATE\u201d appears non-medication.\n\nNext step pending your timing choice:\n- I will post the Observation (status=final; category=laboratory; code.text=\"Medication reconciliation summary\"; subject.reference=Patient/S1733937; valueString as above), and return the full created resource and its id.",
