ccess reason: OH pre-employment clearance).\n\nDe-identified PT/INR order-set template (for OH implementation)\n- Resource: ServiceRequest (configure in your EHR/build tools)\n  - status: active\n  - intent: order\n  - priority: routine\n  - code:\n    - text: \u201cPT/INR (INR)\u201d\n    - Optional codings (confirm with your lab):\n      - LOINC (example): INR 6301-6; PT 5902-2 (or your lab\u2019s preferred codes)\n      - Local lab test code as primary if required\n  - subject: to be populated at order time\n  - authoredOn: set at signing\n  - occurrenceDateTime: set per scheduling (\u201cas soon as possible\u201d)\n  - note (free text examples; adapt to local fields/workflows):\n    - \u201cReason/Indication: Occupational Health pre-employment clearance \u2014 per patient authorization.\u201d\n    - \u201cRequester: Occupational Health.\u201d\n    - \u201cRouting: Send results to OCC HEALTH RESULTS; maintain OH-LIMITED privacy.\u201d\n    - \u201cAuthorized by [Authorization ID]; Compliance [Ticket ID].\u201d\n- Additional build considerations\n  - Associate to the OH encounter at order time.\n  - Default routing to OH results pool; suppress external in-basket per policy.\n  - Do not auto-update problem list or send patient-facing messages for this order set.\n  - Include decision-support reminder: \u201cOrder only if no INR within 30 days or latest INR outside 2.0\u20133.0.\u201d\n\nOptional implementation notes\n- Query logic (for builders): \n  - Medications: active MedicationRequest where medication text or code maps to warfarin.\n  - Labs: Observations category=laboratory with code/text containing \u201cINR,\u201d effective date within 90 days, status=final; pick most recent.\n- QA checks:\n  - Validate routing and privacy flags in test environment.\n  - Audit that no external messaging is triggered from this order.\n  - Confirm fallback handling for multiple INRs on same day (choose latest final).\n\nIf you\u2019d like, I can tailor the template text field