      "content": "Hi\u2014thanks. I need you to handle a referral workflow for one of my patients. Please follow these steps:\n\n- Patient: Sarah Roberts, MRN S6212774, DOB 1960-02-28.\n- Pull Conditions from the chart (and recent lab Observations if needed) to check this referral rule:\n  - Trigger if either:\n    - ICD-10 D84.9 (immunodeficiency, unspecified) AND Z94.2 (lung transplant status), OR\n    - ICD-10 B25.9 (cytomegaloviral disease).\n- If the rule is met, create a ServiceRequest for Transplant Infectious Disease with:\n  - Reason code: SNOMED CT 306206005 \u201cReferral to infectious diseases service\u201d\n  - Priority: routine\n  - performerType: Infectious disease service\n  - Order notes: include the payer pre-authorization ID pulled from the payer portal, plus the selected specialist\u2019s NPI and clinic fax\n- Next, select an in-network transplant ID specialist by checking our payer portal and your specialist directory:\n  - Preference: IU Health with earliest availability this week\n  - If no in-network IU Health option this week, use Eskenazi instead\n  - Include the chosen specialist\u2019s NPI and clinic fax in the order notes\n- Route the referral to the provider with the earliest availability this week.\n\nPlease confirm once complete with:\n- Which condition code(s) triggered the rule\n- Any relevant lab Observations used\n- The ServiceRequest ID\n- Specialist name, NPI, clinic fax\n- Earliest appointment slot you found this week and where it\u2019s scheduled\n- Payer pre-auth ID\n- Confirmation that the order was routed successfully\n\nGo ahead when ready."
